title:: BMMultichannelPluginSpec
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - a specification for creating a BMMultichannelPlugin
categories:: Classes

Description::

Instances of BMMultichannelPluginSpec serve as templates for creating a link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPlugin:: of a particular type, e.g. an ambisonic decoder, a VBAP panner, etc. They provide functions for such things as link::Classes/SynthDef:: and GUI creation, standard presets, etc. Plugin specs allow for user customisation at plugin creation time through the use of attributes (see below).

Specs are stored in a global dictionary held in the class variable strong::*specs::. You can see a list of all available specs as follows:

code::
BMMultichannelPluginSpec.specs.keys;
::

See also: link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPlugin::, link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPluginsRack::, link::Classes/Plugins/BMPluginSpec::, link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeakerSpec::

Section:: BMPlugin vs. BMMultichannelPlugin

BMPlugin is monophonic, i.e. it has a single input and output, which are in fact the same bus. BMMultichannelPlugins can have variable numbers of inputs and outputs, which need not match. The exact number and configuration of inputs and outputs expected varies according to the multichannel plugin's spec. Some specs require inputs and outputs in a specified order, others (e.g. VBAP panners) depend on speaker position data.

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new BMMultichannelPluginSpec and add it to strong::*specs::. If a spec with this strong::name:: already exists it will be replaced.

argument:: name
A link::Classes/Symbol:: indicating the name of this plugin spec.
argument:: ugenGraphFunc
A link::Classes/Function:: detailing this spec's processing chain. When a plugin is created this will be passed the link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPlugin:: instance, strong::numInputs::, strong::numOutputs::, and its input signal(s) as its first four arguments. (If inputs.size > 1 the input signals will be an link::Classes/Array::, otherwise just a single signal.) Additional arguments will result in instances of link::Classes/Control:: being created. The default GUI function uses the order these are listed to determine order in the GUI.
argument:: specsDict
A link::Classes/Dictionary:: or subclass matching link::Classes/Control:: names as keys with instances of link::Classes/ControlSpec::. Plugin instances make a copy of this which can be modified when strong::setupFunc:: (see below) is called. These will be used in GUI construction.
argument:: guiFunc
An optional link::Classes/Function:: which will be used to create GUIs for plugin instances using this spec. This Function will be passed the plugin instance as an argument, and should return the GUI's window. If nil is passed here, a default GUI Function will be used.
argument:: presets
An optional link::Classes/Dictionary:: or subclass providing parameter presets. Keys are Symbols indicating preset names, values are Dictionaries or subclasses matching Control names to values.
argument:: description
A link::Classes/String:: to serve as a human readable description of this spec.
argument:: defaultAttributes
Plugin specs can optionally provide a set of overridable attributes which can serve as settings or inputs to their strong::ugenGraphFunc::, strong::guiFunc::, strong::setupFunc::, and strong::cleanupFunc::. This should be a link::Classes/Dictionary:: or subclass containing key value pairs. Users can override these defaults by passing a Dictionary or subclass as the strong::attributes:: argument to strong::BMMultichannelPlugin:new::. 
argument:: inRange
An link::Classes/Array:: in the form [minNumInputs, maxNumInputs] specifying the number of allowable inputs. The default is [1, inf].
argument:: outRange
An Array in the form [minNumOutputs, maxNumOutputs] specifying the number of allowable outputs. The default is [1, inf].
argument:: setupFunc
An optional link::Classes/Function:: that will be evaluated when a plugin instance is made, and before strong::ugenGraphFunc:: is evaluated. It will be passed the plugin instance as an argument. It can store any objects created in strong::attributes:: for use by the strong::ugenGraphFunc::, strong::guiFunc::, or strong::cleanUpFunc::. It can also do things like modify the plugin's local copy of the strong::specsDict::.
argument:: cleanupFunc
An optional link::Classes/Function:: that will be evaluated when a plugin instance is released. It will be passed the plugin instance as an argument.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

method:: specs
Returns an link::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: containing all currently existing specs. This uses the names of specs as Symbols for keys.
		
code::
BMMultichannelPluginSpec.specs['B-Format Decoder'];
::
				
method:: maxInputs
Returns the maximum number of inputs for plugins using this spec.
				
method:: minInputs
Returns the minimum number of inputs for plugins using this spec.
				
method:: maxOutputs
Returns the maximum number of outputs for plugins using this spec.
				
method:: minOutputs
Returns the minimum number of outputs for plugins using this spec.
				
method:: setupFunc
Returns this spec's strong::setupFunc:: (see above).
				
method:: cleanupFunc
Returns this spec's strong::cleanupFunc:: (see above).
				
method:: ugenGraphFunc
Returns this spec's strong::ugenGraphFunc:: (see above).

method:: guiFunc
Returns this spec's strong::guiFunc:: (see above) if one has been provided, or the default GUI function otherwise.
				
method:: description
Returns a link::Classes/String:: which serves as a human readable description of this spec.
				
method:: presets
Set or get this spec's strong::presets:: dictionary.
				
method:: defaultAttributes
Returns this spec's strong::defaultAttributes:: (see above).
				
method:: specsDict
Returns this spec's strong::specsDict:: (see above). Plugins may customize specDicts in their strong::setupFunc::, so when working with a plugin, use its strong::specsDict:: getter method rather than this one.
				
	name
		
		Returns this spec's name as a Symbol.
					
				
Examples

////// some plugin spec examples (see the *initClass method for more)

(
BMMultichannelPluginSpec('Help-2D VBAP Panner', 			// name
	{|plugin, numInputs, numOutputs, inputs, azimuth, spread, azimuthLag| // ugenGraphFunc
		VBAP.ar(
			numOutputs, 
			inputs,
			plugin.attributes[\buffer],
			azimuth.circleRamp(azimuthLag), 
			0,
			spread
		);
	}, 								
	(azimuth: [-180, 180, 'lin', 0.0,  0, " deg"].asSpec,		// specsDict
	spread: [0, 100, 'lin', 0.0, 2, " %"].asSpec,
	azimuthLag: [0, 1, 'lin', 0.0, 0.1, " sec"].asSpec
	),				
	nil, 												// use default GUI
	('dead ahead': (azimuth: 0)), 							// presets
	"Mono input 2D Vector Base Amplitude Panner",				// description
	nil, 								// use defaultAttributes
	[1, 1],								// inRange
	[2, inf],								// outRange 
	{|plugin| 							// setupFunc
		var speakers;
		speakers = plugin.outputs.collectAs({|out|
			out.isBMSpeaker.not.if({
				"VBAP output not a speaker".error;
				^false;
			});
			out.azi;
		}, Array);
		speakers = VBAPSpeakerArray(2, speakers);
		plugin.attributes[\buffer] = 
			Buffer.loadCollection(plugin.server, speakers.getSetsAndMatrices);
	},								
	{|plugin|								// cleanupFunc
		plugin.attributes[\buffer].free;
	}								
);
)

// This one uses setupFunc to modify the plugin's local specsDict copy based on the number of outputs

BMMultichannelPluginSpec('Help-Xfade Seq', // name
	{|plugin, numInputs, numOutputs, inputs, position, width| // ugenGraphFunc
		PanAz.ar(
			numOutputs, 
			inputs, 
			position * 2.0, 
			1, 
			width, 
			0.0
		);
	}, 								
	(position: [0.0, 1.0, 'lin', 0.0, 0.0].asSpec, // specsDict
	width: nil // placeholder (not really needed)
	),				
	nil, 							// use default GUI
	nil, 							// presets
	"Crossfade a signal through a looped sequence of channels\nOrder corresponds with order of outputs\nPosition cycles between 0 and 1\nWidth is number of channels simultaneously active, i.e. 2 = stereo", // description
	nil, 						// use defaultAttributes
	[1, 1],						// inRange
	[2, inf],						// outRange
	{|plugin|						// setupFunc modifies specsDict
		plugin.specsDict[\width] = [2.0, plugin.numOutputs, 'lin', 0.0,  2.0].asSpec;
	}		
);
